responding and I hadn't.

00:06:14.653 --> 00:06:16.800
Yes nobody was responding.

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:19.070
It was, I fell asleep.

00:06:19.070 --> 00:06:20.810
- [Interviewer] All
your connections were--

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:24.090
- Yeah, I lost, I lost my last phone,

00:06:24.090 --> 00:06:25.860
and lost my girl's phone,

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:26.800
so all contacts--

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:28.250
- [Interviewer] So all
your contacts were gone?

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:31.890
- Yeah and I just lost an
iPad out here on skid row.

00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:33.890
- [Interviewer] you lose things
on a daily basis out here.

00:06:33.890 --> 00:06:36.560
- Yeah, absolutely do, absolutely do.

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:37.393
- [Interviewer] And living on the streets,

00:06:37.393 --> 00:06:39.137
I mean that lifestyle works for you?

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:43.260
- Honestly for a certain
amount of time I enjoy it

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:44.093
because it's not like

00:06:44.093 --> 00:06:47.100
because that's all I knew,
you know, since a young age,

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:50.600
I was either in institutions
or on the streets, you know,

00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:52.540
I didn't know how to live a regular life.

00:06:52.540 --> 00:06:55.940
Go to work everyday, pay your
bills, that type of stuff.

00:06:55.940 --> 00:06:57.770
You know, since I came
out here to California,

00:06:57.770 --> 00:07:01.050
after getting sober for a
while, I started living that.

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:04.170
But, and for me and my fiance,

00:07:04.170 --> 00:07:05.050
I don't want that for us,

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:07.759
