00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:20.240
- It not only scares me.

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:23.840
I don't know if I can handle it, you know?

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:28.160
Yeah I mean, I've been doing
all right, but it's the drugs,

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:31.130
always, everything goes away,
everything will go away,

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:34.010
everything that we have
booked up for so long,

00:07:34.010 --> 00:07:35.970
it all goes away in the end.

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:38.120
You know, this is ground zero.

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:39.621
This is where you ended
up every single time,

00:07:39.621 --> 00:07:40.733
no matter what.

00:07:41.950 --> 00:07:43.230
- [Interviewer] You think
you'll end up spending

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:47.050
the rest of your life on,
in this kind of situation?

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:48.560
- Well I'm not lucky enough

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:50.754
to die from using fentanyl.

00:07:50.754 --> 00:07:53.543
'Cause I was, once you
build a tolerance, you know,

00:07:53.543 --> 00:07:55.700
there's no overdosing anymore,

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:58.780
no matter how you try,
it just doesn't work.

00:07:58.780 --> 00:07:59.613
- [Interviewer] Oh really?

00:07:59.613 --> 00:08:01.980
So because your body has
built a tolerance to it

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:03.710
you can do more and more of it?

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:05.860
- Yeah I mean, you just do a lot.

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:07.700
I mean there's always a chance that like

00:08:07.700 --> 00:08:08.630
you'll do the one shot

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:10.030
that'll kill you, but--

00:08:10.030 --> 00:08:12.010
- [Interviewer] And is there a high still

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:13.740
from doing fentanyl?

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:15.180
- For a while, there, there isn't,

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:17.373
but there's like different
types of fentanyl,

00:08:17.373 --> 00:08:18.790
there's carfentanil,

00:08:18.790 --> 00:08:20.890
there's irregular fentanyl,
the dark burning stuff,

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:22.340
and that's more like a body high

00:08:22.340 --> 00:08:23.550
it lasts a little bit longer

00:08:23.550 --> 00:08:25.460
and I don't really get high from it, but--

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:26.293
- [Interviewer] You just need it?

00:08:26.293 --> 00:08:27.600
- I need, I feel well from it.

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:31.260
But the carfentanil
knocks you out, you know,

00:08:31.260 --> 00:08:32.260
it'll knock you out.

00:08:33.770 --> 00:08:37.780
But no, I'm not really
scared of it anymore.

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:41.327
Like I used to, used to be, you know,

00:08:41.327 --> 00:08:42.930
and there's times where I don't

00:08:42.930 --> 00:08:45.660
I've almost, I probably
blackout every night.

00:08:45.660 --> 00:08:46.810
Like if I stay up for a couple of days,

00:08:46.810 --> 00:08:50.090
I won't know how, I'll go to sleep.

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:51.360
Me and my fiance will both pass out

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:53.629
